---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { env } from 'cloudflare:workers';
const contactEnabled = env.CONTACT_ENABLED === 'true';
---
<Layout title="About & Contact" active="none" description="Publisher information, editorial standards, and contact details for ENSOLens, an independent ENSO data and climate context project.">
  <div class="page-shell subpage prose-page"><div class="page-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">PUBLISHER</span><h1>About <span>ENSOLens.</span></h1><p>An independent climate data and context project.</p></div></div>
  <section class="method-section"><h2>Who publishes this site</h2><p>ENSOLens is an independently operated ENSO information project. It is not affiliated with NOAA, CPC, or any government agency. ENSOLens is responsible for this site's presentation, source processing, and editorial context; NOAA and CPC remain the original sources of the official observations and forecasts.</p></section>
  <section class="method-section"><h2>Editorial standards</h2><p>We distinguish observations, official outlooks, and historical context. Source dates remain visible, comparisons refer to the same target season, and unverified values are not substituted for official data. Failed source checks retain the last validated values with a visible notice. Material data corrections follow the revised source publication.</p><p>Read the <a href="/methodology/">sources and methodology</a> for index definitions and update handling. This site provides general climate information. Use official local forecasts and warnings for decisions about immediate weather hazards.</p></section>
  <section class="method-section"><h2>How editorial work is checked</h2><p>ENSOLens uses AI assistance for research, drafting, diagrams and code. The publisher remains responsible for what is published. Source checks compare specific claims, issue dates, target seasons and index definitions with the named original products. Build and browser tests check delivery and interactions; they do not certify scientific accuracy.</p><p>Independent reviews, when available, are limited to the material actually reviewed. We do not claim that every sentence has been reviewed by a climate scientist or that an automated check is expert peer review. Conceptual diagrams and invented teaching values are labeled separately from official observations. Source review dates and substantive modification dates are recorded separately.</p></section>
  <section class="method-section" aria-labelledby="corrections-heading"><h2 id="corrections-heading">Report a content error</h2><p>Use this form for a factual error, broken source or misleading chart. Include the affected observation or issue date and original source URL in the explanation. Do not include your name, email, private information or emergency reports. Submissions are private and do not receive personal replies. See our <a href="/privacy/">data handling policy</a>.</p>
  <form class="correction-form" action="/api/corrections/" method="post">
    <label for="correction-page">ENSOLens page path</label><input id="correction-page" name="page" required maxlength="240" placeholder="/forecast/" />
    <label for="correction-explanation">What should be corrected, and why?</label><textarea id="correction-explanation" name="explanation" required minlength="15" maxlength="2000" rows="7"></textarea>
    <div class="form-trap" aria-hidden="true"><label>Leave empty<input name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" /></label></div>
    <button type="submit">Send correction report</button>
  </form></section>
  <section class="method-section" aria-labelledby="correction-log-heading"><h2 id="correction-log-heading">Material correction log</h2><ul><li><time datetime="2026-11-13">November 13, 2026</time>: corrected the FAQ’s implication that La Niña creates hyperactive Atlantic seasons; narrowed Pacific geography and added other drivers and a direct NOAA mechanism source.</li><li><time datetime="2026-11-13">November 13, 2026</time>: replaced a historical page’s October-issue citation to a rolling discussion with a preserved, dated November reference. Added delayed-source disclosure and observation-year handling to that comparison.</li><li><time datetime="2026-11-13">November 13, 2026</time>: removed rigid event-onset/decay month claims and unsupported broad regional drought attribution from the duration FAQ. Added task-specific teaching diagrams and comparisons to the learning library.</li></ul><p>Smaller wording, layout and navigation changes are not individually listed. Official source revisions remain distinct from corrections to our explanations.</p></section>
  <section class="method-section"><h2>Publisher inquiries</h2>{contactEnabled ? <p>For data corrections, source questions, and publisher inquiries, email <a href="mailto:contact@ensolens.com">contact@ensolens.com</a>. Include the page URL, relevant observation or forecast date, and the original source where possible.</p> : <p>A dedicated contact mailbox is being set up. Contact details will be published here after delivery has been verified.</p>}</section>
  <p class="figure-note">Editorial process and corrections updated November 13, 2026. <a href="/privacy/">Privacy policy</a></p></div>
</Layout>

<style>
#corrections-heading,#correction-log-heading { scroll-margin-top:110px; }
.correction-form { display:grid; gap:12px; margin:24px 0; max-width:700px; }
.correction-form input,.correction-form textarea { width:100%; box-sizing:border-box; background:var(--card); color:var(--ink); border:1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius:6px; padding:12px; font:inherit; }
.correction-form button { justify-self:start; padding:14px 20px; border:1px solid var(--green); background:var(--green); color:#08221a; border-radius:6px; cursor:pointer; }
.form-trap { position:absolute; left:-10000px; width:1px; height:1px; overflow:hidden; }
.method-section li { line-height:1.9; margin:16px 0; }
</style>
